+## Durable message metadata
+
+Attach application-owned JSON data to a user message when UI choices must survive reloads:
+
+```ts
+const { session } = await client.sessions.create({
+  message: "Draft a document.",
+  messageMetadata: { editor: { selectedTool: "canvas" } },
+});
+await session.send("Continue normally.", {
+  messageMetadata: { editor: { selectedTool: null } },
+});
+```
+
+The HTTP create and message routes accept the same `messageMetadata` object.
+`message.received.data.metadata` contains it, and the default message reducer exposes
+it as `EveMessage.metadata.custom`. Each message owns its metadata: omitting the
+field on a later message does not inherit an earlier value. JSON null values are
+preserved. Response-only requests cannot carry message metadata.
+
+Metadata is durable display/application data. eve never includes it in model
+prompts, treats it as authentication, or lets its keys override framework fields
+such as `turnId` and `status`. Validate your application's namespace before using
+it. Do not store secrets in metadata: users who can read the transcript can read it.
+
+Server-authorized transcript seeds accept `metadata?: JsonObject` on each user or
+assistant message. Copy `message.metadata.custom` into that seed field to preserve
+original UI choices; imported-prefix forks preserve it too. When a channel
+coalesces multiple deliveries into one user message, the last message's metadata
+wins, even when omitted; control-only deliveries do not overwrite it.
+
+Metadata requires inbox wire v8 and appears in stream v27. A metadata-bearing send
+to an older inbox consumer fails explicitly instead of silently dropping data.
